# 9. Add Rate Limiting

Apply server-side rate limits to:
- Login and authentication attempts.
- Password reset requests.
- Registration, if available.
- Document uploads.
- OCR and document extraction.
- Expensive AI requests.
- Report generation.
- Public forms and other abuse-prone endpoints.

Requirements:
- Use appropriate per-IP and per-account limits.
- Use shared storage for limits in multi-instance deployments.
- Return appropriate HTTP 429 responses.
- Provide a reasonable retry message.
- Avoid revealing sensitive account information.
- Add request-size limits, timeouts, and resource controls.
- Ensure rate limits cannot be trivially bypassed by changing client-side values.

Do not add rate-limit UI without enforcing limits on the server.

